/*
==================================================
Problem Number : 1342
Problem Name   : Number of Steps to Reduce a Number to Zero
Difficulty     : Easy

Topics
- Math
- Bit Manipulation
- Simulation

Pattern
- Simulation
- Conditional Processing

Approach
- Initialize a counter to keep track of the number of steps.
- Repeat until the number becomes zero:
  - If the number is even, divide it by 2.
  - Otherwise, subtract 1.
- Increment the counter after every operation.
- Return the total number of steps.

Time Complexity
O(log n)

Space Complexity
O(1)

Learning
- Even numbers can be efficiently reduced by dividing by 2.
- Odd numbers must first become even by subtracting 1.
- Each iteration reduces the number significantly, leading to logarithmic complexity.
- This problem can also be solved using bit manipulation.

==================================================
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int numberOfSteps(int num) {
        int count = 0;

        while (num > 0) {
            if (num % 2 == 0) {
                num /= 2;
                count++;
            }
            else {
                num -= 1;
                count++;
            }
        }

        return count;
    }
};
